remuneration
InquiryPayEquity
/
remuneration
Definition
Details about the remuneration package, including salary tables based on the work duration. It includes one or more salary tables for a specific work duration or characteristics.
Type
RemunerationPackage
https://ontology.setu.nl/inquiry-pay-equity#RemunerationPackage
Usage notes
The remuneration block provides the ability to define a salary table, including the associated scales, steps, the conditions under which an employee becomes eligible, and salary increases.

For example:

A salary table based on a 40‑hour work week with two salary scales, each containing three different steps. The scales apply to one or more roles within the organisation. Compensation is determined on a monthly basis.

In this example, work experience is also considered when determining the appropriate scale. Additionally, there is a one‑time salary increase of 5 percent on 01‑01‑2026, applied to the annual salary based on performance.

